              "uco-observable:stringValue": "Query Reports Utilities Help Log Out\n\nRESTR,2255,BradyAd,PSLCT\n\nU.S. District Court\nUnited States District Court for the District of Alaska (Anchorage)\nCRIMINAL DOCKET FOR CASE #: 3:19-cr-00003-RRB-MMS All Defendants\n\nCase title: USA v. Grant Date Filed: 01/15/2019\n\nMagistrate judge case number: 3:18-mj-00581-MMS Date Terminated: 01/13/2022\n\nAssigned to: Ralph R. Beistline\nReferred to: Matthew McCrary Scoble\nAppeals court case number: 22-30071 9CCA\n\nDefendant (1)\nTristan Grant represented by Jay A. Nelson\n35297-183 Law Office of Jay A. Nelson\nTERMINATED: 01/13/2022 637 SW Keck Drive, No 415\nalso known as McMinnville, OR 97128\nGoo 503-857-0873\nTERMINATED: 01/13/2022 Fax: 503-419-4371\nEmail: jay@jayanelson.com\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: CJA Appointment\n\nKathleen Bliss\nKathleen Bliss Law PLLC\n170 South Green Valley Parkway\nSuite 300\nHenderson, NV 89012\n702-318-7375\nEmail: kb@kathleenblisslaw.com\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: CJA Appointment\n\nMichael Alexander Marks\nAlaska Federal Public Defender\n188 W. Northern Lights Blvd.\nSuite 700\nAnchorage, AK 99503\n907-646-3400\nEmail: michael_marks@fd.org\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Federal Public Defender\n\nBrian D. Heady\nLaw Office Brian Heady\n205 E. Benson Blvd., Suite 102\nAnchorage, AK 99503\n907-868-1932\nFax: 907-8681942\nEmail: bheady@headylawoffice.com\nTERMINATED: 10/26/2020\nDesignation: CJA Appointment\n\nD. Scott Dattan\nLaw Office of D. Scott Dattan\n341 West Tudor Road, Suite 103\nAnchorage, AK 99503\n907-276-8008\nFax: 907-278-8571\nEmail: dattan@dattanlaw.com\nTERMINATED: 03/31/2020\nDesignation: CJA Appointment\n\nDarla J. Mondou\nMondou Law Office\n2388 S. Orchard View Dr.\nGreen Valley, AZ 85614\n520-241-7392\nFax: 707-276-1158\nEmail: darlalaw@aol.com\nTERMINATED: 09/14/2022\nDesignation: CJA Appointment\n\nJames A. Wendt\nLaw Offices of James Alan Wendt\n425 G Street, Suite 610\nAnchorage, AK 99501\n907-258-9100\nFax: 907-258-7329\nEmail: jawlaw@ak.net\nTERMINATED: 06/13/2022\nDesignation: CJA Appointment\n\nJamie McGrady\nFederal Public Defender Office\n188 West Northern Lights Blvd. Suite 700\nAnchorage, AK 99503\n907-646-3400\nEmail: jamie_mcgrady@fd.org\nTERMINATED: 02/02/2026\nDesignation: Federal Public Defender\n\nSamuel J. Fortier\nFortier & Mikko, P.C.\nLIMITED APPEARANCE\n1600 A Street, Suite 101\nAnchorage, AK 99501\n907-277-4222\nFax: 907-277-4221\nEmail: sfortier@fortiermikko.com\nTERMINATED: 03/09/2021\nDesignation: CJA Appointment\n\nSteven M. Wells\nSteven M. Wells, PC\n431 West 7th Avenue, Suite 107\nAnchorage, AK 99501\n907-279-3557\nFax: 907-279-3558\nEmail: steve@alaskalegaldefense.com\nTERMINATED: 10/21/2020\nDesignation: CJA Appointment\n\nPending Counts Disposition\n18:1594(c) CONSPIRACY TO ENGAGE IN SEX Counts 1ssss - 10ssss: 420 months imprisonment; Life\nTRAFFICKING OF MINORS supervised release; $1,000 special assessment. Defendant to\n(1ssss) forfeit interest in the property to the United States as directed.\nCounts 1ssss - 10ssss: 420 months imprisonment; Life\n18:1591 SEX TRAFFICKING OF A MINOR\nsupervised release; $1,000 special assessment. Defendant to\n(2ssss-5ssss)\nforfeit interest in the property to the United States as directed.\n18:2251(a),(e) SEXUAL EXPLOITATION OF A CHILD- Counts 1ssss - 10ssss: 420 months imprisonment; Life\nPRODUCTION OF CHILD PORNOGRAPHY supervised release; $1,000 special assessment. Defendant to\n(6ssss-8ssss) forfeit interest in the property to the United States as directed.\n18:922(g)(1) and 924(a)(2) FELON IN POSSESSION OF Counts 1ssss - 10ssss: 420 months imprisonment; Life\nFIREARM AND AMMUNITION supervised release; $1,000 special assessment. Defendant to\n(9ssss-10ssss) forfeit interest in the property to the United States as directed.\n\nHighest Offense Level (Opening)\nFelony\n\nTerminated Counts Disposition\n18:922(g)(1) and 924(a)(2) FELON IN POSSESSION OF\nFIREARM AND AMMUNITION\n(1-2)\n18:922(g)(1) and 924(a)(2) FELON IN POSSESSION OF\nFIREARM AND AMMUNITION\n(1s-2s)\n18:922(g)(1) and 924(a)(2) FELON IN POSSESSION OF\nFIREARM AND AMMUNITION\n(1ss-2ss)\n18:922(g)(1) and 924(a)(2) FELON IN POSSESSION OF A\nFIREARM AND AMMUNITION\n(1sss-2sss)\n18:2251(a)and(e) SEXUAL EXPLOITATION OF A CHILD-\nPRODUCTION OF CHILD PORNOGRAPHY\n(3s)\n18:2251(a) and (e) SEXUAL EXPLOITATION OF A CHILD-\nPRODUCTION OF CHILD PORNOGRAPHY\n(3ss)\n18:2251(a)and (e) SEXUAL EXPLOITATION OF A CHILD-\nPRODUCTION OF CHILD PORNOGRAHPY\n(3sss-5sss)\n\nHighest Offense Level (Terminated)\nFelony\n\nComplaints Disposition\n18:922(g)(1) Possession of a firearm or ammunition by a\nprohibited person\nPlaintiff\nUSA represented by Jennifer Lowe Ivers\nU.S. Attorney's Office (Anch)\n222 West 7th Avenue, RM 253 #9\nAnchorage, AK 99513\n907-271-1555\nFax: 907-271-1500\nEmail: Jennifer.Ivers@usdoj.gov\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Assistant US Attorney\n\nKayla Hayes Doyle\nUnited States Attorney's Office Anchorage\n222 West 7th Avenue\nAnchorage, AK 99513\n907-250-7710\nEmail: kayla.doyle@alaska.gov\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Assistant US Attorney\n\nAnne Johnson Veldhuis\nDOJ-Atr\n450 Golden Gate Avenue\nRoom 10-0101\nSan Francisco, CA 94102\n415-307-6722\nEmail: anne.veldhuis@usdoj.gov\nDesignation: Assistant US Attorney\n\nKelly A. Cavanaugh\nU.S. Attorney's Office (Anc)\n222 West Seventh, Ave, #9, Room 253\nAnchorage, AK 99513\n907-271-5071\nFax: 907-271-1500\nEmail: xkelly.cavanaugh@usdoj.gov\nTERMINATED: 01/31/2022\nDesignation: Assistant US Attorney\n\nKyle Frederick Reardon\nU.S. Attorney's Office (Anc)\n222 West Seventh, Ave, #9, Room 253\nAnchorage, AK 99513\n907-271-3389\nFax: 907-271-1500\nEmail: xkyle.reardon@usdoj.gov\nDesignation: Assistant US Attorney\n\nSeth M. Beausang\nU.S. Attorney's Office (Anc)\n222 West Seventh, Ave, #9, Room 253\nAnchorage, AK 99513\n907-271-3378\nFax: 907-271-2344\nEmail: seth.beausang@usdoj.gov\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\n\nDate Filed # Docket Text\n12/18/2018 1 COMPLAINT as to Tristan Grant (1). (Attachments: # 1 Affidavit) (BJK, COURT STAFF) [3:18-mj-00581-MMS] (Entered: 12/19/2018)\n12/19/2018 Notice of Arrest of Tristan Grant. Defendant arrested 12/18/2018. (BJK, COURT STAFF) Modified on 12/19/2018 to reflect defendant is\nin state custody. (BJK, COURT STAFF). [3:18-mj-00581-MMS] (Entered: 12/19/2018)\n12/19/2018 Notice of Defendant in State Custody re Tristan Grant. Defendant is being held at Anchorage Jail. (BJK, COURT STAFF) [3:18-mj-\n00581-MMS] (Entered: 12/19/2018)\n12/19/2018 2 MMS TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: Initial Appearance on Complaint/Detention Hearing set for 12/21/2018 at 9:30 AM in\nAnchorage Courtroom 6 before Matthew McCrary Scoble. (BJK, COURT STAFF) [3:18-mj-00581-MMS] (Entered: 12/19/2018)\n12/20/2018 3 PRETRIAL SERVICES REPORT (Sealed) as to Tristan Grant. (Moua, Yang) [3:18-mj-00581-MMS] (Entered: 12/20/2018)\n12/20/2018 4 MOTION for Writ of Habeas Corpus ad prosequendum by USA as to Tristan Grant. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Writ, # 2 Proposed\nOrder)(Reardon, Kyle) [3:18-mj-00581-MMS] (Entered: 12/20/2018)\n12/20/2018 6 ORDER granting 4 Motion for Writ of Habeas Corpus ad prosequendum as to Tristan Grant (1). Signed by Judge Deborah M. Smith on\n12/20/2018. (BJK, COURT STAFF) [3:18-mj-00581-MMS] (Entered: 12/20/2018)\n12/20/2018 Writ of Habeas Corpus ad Prosequendum Issued as to Tristan Grant. Orig +1 cert copy to USM. (BJK, COURT STAFF) [3:18-mj-00581-\nMMS] (Entered: 12/20/2018)\n12/20/2018 7 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE: D. Scott Dattan appearing for Tristan Grant (Dattan, D.) [3:18-mj-00581-MMS] (Entered:\n12/20/2018)\n12/20/2018 8 First MOTION to Continue Arraignment Unopposed on Shortened Time by Tristan Grant. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Dattan, D.)\n[3:18-mj-00581-MMS] (Entered: 12/20/2018)\n12/20/2018 9 MMS TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: Motion to Continue Arraignment 8 is DENIED. Defense counsel is not officially appointed and\nis directed to contact the CJA Administrator. (JBO, CHAMBERS STAFF) [3:18-mj-00581-MMS] (Entered: 12/20/2018)\n12/21/2018 10 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Matthew McCrary Scoble: Initial Appearance on Complaint/Detention Hearing as to\nTristan Grant held 9:44 a.m. to 9:55 a.m. 12/21/2018. Copy of Complaint given to defendant; summarized. Defendant stated true name: as\nsame. Defendant advised of general rights, charges and penalties. Waiver of Preliminary Hearing to be filed by 12/28/2018. Court directed\nclerk to vacate Preliminary Hearing upon receipt of Waiver. Preliminary Examination set for 1/4/2019 01:00 PM in Anchorage Courtroom\n6 before Matthew McCrary Scoble. Court and counsel heard re defendant's Detention. Defendant had no bail proposal at this time. Court\nordered defendant's detention. APPEARANCES: Defendant Present, In Custody; Kyle Frederick Reardon, AUSA; D. Scott Dattan, CJA;\nYang D. Moua, USPO. cc: FPD (CJA CLERK) (ACW, COURT STAFF) [3:18-mj-00581-MMS] (Entered: 12/21/2018)\n12/21/2018 11 CJA 23 Financial Affidavit by Tristan Grant. (ACW, COURT STAFF) [3:18-mj-00581-MMS] (Entered: 12/21/2018)\n12/21/2018 12 ORDER OF DETENTION PENDING HEARING as to Tristan Grant Signed by Judge Matthew McCrary Scoble on 12/21/2018. (ACW,\nCOURT STAFF) [3:18-mj-00581-MMS] (Entered: 12/21/2018)\n12/26/2018 13 CLERK'S NOTICE as to Tristan Grant: By agreement of the judges this matter is hereby reassigned to the Honorable Matthew M. Scoble.\nPlease use the following case number on all future filings: 3:18-mj-00581-MMS. (BJK, COURT STAFF) [3:18-mj-00581-MMS] (Entered:\n12/26/2018)\n12/27/2018 14 Arrest Warrant Returned Executed on 12/21/2018 in case as to Tristan Grant. (BJK, COURT STAFF) [3:18-mj-00581-MMS] (Entered:\n12/28/2018)\n12/31/2018 15 MMS TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: Due to court calendar conflict, the Preliminary Examination set for 1/4/2019 at 1:00 PM is\nhereby VACATED and RESET for 1/4/2019 at 11:00 AM in Anchorage Courtroom 6 before Matthew McCrary Scoble. (JBO,\nCHAMBERS STAFF) [3:18-mj-00581-MMS] (Entered: 12/31/2018)\n01/04/2019 16 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Matthew McCrary Scoble: Status Conference (Preliminary Hearing) as to Tristan Grant\nheld 11:08 a.m. to 11:14 a.m. on 1/4/2019. Court and counsel heard re defendant's intent to waive preliminary hearing and further\nproceedings in this matter. Waiver of Preliminary Hearing FILED. Status Conference set for 1/22/2019 11:00 AM in Anchorage\nCourtroom 6 before Matthew McCrary Scoble. Court and counsel heard re defendant's Oral Motion to Appear Telephonic at Status\nConference 1/22/2019; GRANTED. Mr. Dattan to call 1-866-434-5269, access code: 4271682, five minutes prior to the hearing start time\nfrom a landline. Detention continued. APPEARANCES: Defendant Present, In Custody; Kyle Frederick Reardon, AUSA; D. Scott Dattan,\nCJA. (ACW, COURT STAFF) [3:18-mj-00581-MMS] (Entered: 01/04/2019)\n01/04/2019 17 WAIVER of Preliminary Hearing by Tristan Grant. (ACW, COURT STAFF) (Main Document 17 replaced on 1/4/2019) (ACW, COURT\nSTAFF). [3:18-mj-00581-MMS] (Entered: 01/04/2019)\n01/08/2019 18 MMS TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: Due to a court calendar conflict, the Status Conference set for 1/22/2019 at 11:00 AM is\nhereby VACATED and RESET for the same day at 10:30 AM in Anchorage Courtroom 6 before Matthew McCrary Scoble. (JBO,\nCHAMBERS STAFF) [3:18-mj-00581-MMS] (Entered: 01/08/2019)\n01/15/2019 19 INDICTMENT COVER SHEET(S) AND SIGNATURES as to Tristan Grant (1) count(s) 1-2. (Attachments: # 1 Criminal Cover Sheet re\nDefendant Grant) (BJK, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 01/15/2019)\n01/15/2019 20 INDICTMENT as to Tristan Grant. (BJK, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 01/15/2019)\n01/15/2019 21 MMS TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: The Status Conference previously set in 3:18-mj-00581-MMS is hereby VACATED and\nRESET as an Arraignment on Indictment 20 for 1/22/2019 at 10:30 AM in Anchorage Courtroom 6 before Matthew McCrary Scoble. Mr.\nDattan to call 1-866-434-5269 and enter access code: 4271682# and then # again, five minutes prior to the hearing start time from a\nlandline. (BJK, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 01/15/2019)\n01/16/2019 NOTICE of Availability as to Tristan Grant. (BJK, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 01/16/2019)\n01/22/2019 22 MINUTE ENTRY for proceedings held before Judge Matthew McCrary Scoble: Arraignment on Indictment (DKT 20 ) as to Tristan Grant\n(1) Count 1-2 held 10:33 AM to 10:41 AM on 1/22/2019. Copy of Indictment given to defendant; waived reading. Defendant verified true\nname as same. Defendant advised of general rights, charges and penalties. CJA previously appointed. Defendant pled not guilty to Counts\n1-2 and DENIED any Criminal Forfeiture allegations stated in the Indictment. Trial date and deadlines given. Defendant detained pending\ntrial. APPEARANCES: Defendant present, in-custody; Kyle Frederick Reardon, AUSA; D. Scott Dattan, CJA (Telephonic). (JDS,\nCOURT STAFF) (Entered: 01/22/2019)\n01/22/2019 23 ORDER FOR THE PROGRESSION OF A CRIMINAL CASE as to Tristan Grant: Deadline to Court re: Discovery Issues is 2/18/2019.\nMotions due by 2/18/2019. Final Pretrial Conference set for 3/6/2019 at 9:30 AM in Anchorage Courtroom 2 before Ralph R. Beistline.\nTrial by Jury set for 3/18/2019 at 8:30 AM in Anchorage Courtroom 2 before Ralph R. Beistline. Signed by Judge Matthew McCrary\nScoble on 1/22/2019. (JDS, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 01/22/2019)\n01/22/2019 24 ORDER OF DETENTION PENDING TRIAL as to Tristan Grant. Signed by Judge Matthew McCrary Scoble on 1/22/2019. (JDS,\nCOURT STAFF) (Entered: 01/22/2019)\n02/18/2019 25 First MOTION to Continue Trial by Tristan Grant. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Dattan, D.) (Entered: 02/18/2019)\n02/18/2019 26 First MOTION to Continue Pretrial Motions Deadline by Tristan Grant. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Dattan, D.) (Entered:\n02/18/2019)\n02/19/2019 27 MMS TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: First MOTION to Continue Pretrial Motions Deadline re 26 is held in ABEYANCE pending\nthe District Judge's ruling on the Motion to Continue Trial 25 . (JBO, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 02/19/2019)\n02/19/2019 28 RRB TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: A hearing on Defendant's Motion to Continue Trial at Docket 25 is set for 2/27/2019 at 10:00\na.m. in Anchorage Courtroom 4 before Judge Ralph R. Beistline. cc: USM, USPO. (LLR, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 02/19/2019)\n02/20/2019 29 First MOTION for Hearing Change of Date by Tristan Grant. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Dattan, D.) (Entered: 02/20/2019)\n02/21/2019 30 JUDGE BEISTLINE TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: The Motion to Change Date of Hearing, at docket 29 , is hereby GRANTED.\nThe Hearing on Motion to Continue Trial 25 previously scheduled for 2/27/19 is VACATED and RESET for 2/26/19 at 10:30 AM in\nAnchorage Courtroom 4 before Ralph R. Beistline. (JLH, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 02/21/2019)\n02/26/2019 31 MINUTE ENTRY for proceedings held before Judge Ralph R. Beistline: Hearing on Motion to Continue Trial 25 as to Tristan Grant held\n10:37 AM to 10:46 AM on 2/26/2019. Court and counsel heard re status of discovery, defendant's pending state case, and possible\nsuperseding indictment to follow. First Motion to Continue Trial 25 GRANTED. Court found excludable delay under 18 USC \u00a7 3161(h)\n(7)(B)(i) Failure to continue would stop further proceedings or result in a miscarriage of justice. Final Pretrial Conference set for\n3/06/2019 is VACATED and RESET for 7/18/2019 at 09:00 AM in Anchorage Courtroom 2 before Ralph R. Beistline. Trial by Jury set\nfor 3/18/2019 VACATED and RESET for 7/22/2019 at 08:30 AM in Anchorage Courtroom 2 before Ralph R. Beistline.\nAPPEARANCES: Defendant present, in custody; Kyle Frederick Reardon, AUSA; D. Scott Dattan, CJA. (ECB, COURT STAFF)\n(Entered: 02/26/2019)\n02/28/2019 32 MMS TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: First MOTION to Continue Pretrial Motions Deadline re 26 is GRANTED. Pretria