5/2020. (JBO, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 06/08/2020)\n06/08/2020 97 RRB TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: Pursuant to Miscellaneous General Order 20-17, criminal proceedings are suspended until\n7/6/2020, pending further order of the Court. Therefore, the Final Pretrial Conference and Trial by Jury set for 6/17/2020 and 6/29/2020,\nrespectively, are VACATED and will be reset in due course. Should the parties desire to proceed with a Trial by Court prior to 7/6/2020, a\njoint status report shall be filed, indicating their agreement to proceed by video conference, as well as Defendant's waiver of physical\nappearance. Alternatively, within 14 days of this Order, the parties shall file a request for a new Trial by Jury date with three specific dates\nand times requested. For the reasons stated in Miscellaneous General Order 20-17, the Court finds that the ends of justice served by\nordering a continuance in this case outweigh the best interests of the public and Defendant's right to a speedy trial, pursuant to 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\n3161(h)(7)(A), (B)(i), and (B)(iv). Accordingly, the period of the exclusion shall be from March 16, 2020, through July 6, 2020. cc: USM,\nUSPO. (LLR, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 06/08/2020)\n06/17/2020 99 STATUS REPORT by Tristan Grant (Wells, Steven) (Entered: 06/17/2020)\n06/17/2020 100 RRB TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: A Scheduling Conference is hereby set for 7/15/2020 at 11:00 a.m. in Anchorage Courtroom 2\nbefore Judge Ralph R. Beistline. cc: USM, USPO. (LLR, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 06/17/2020)\n07/09/2020 101 MOTION for Release from Custody by Tristan Grant. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Wells, Steven) (Entered: 07/09/2020)\n07/09/2020 102 RRB TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: Pursuant to Miscellaneous General Order 20-24, criminal proceedings are suspended until\n9/4/2020, pending further order of the Court. Therefore, the Scheduling Conference set for 7/15/2020 is VACATED and a Telephonic\nScheduling Conference will be set in due course. For the reasons stated in Miscellaneous General Order 20-24, the Court finds that the\nends of justice served by ordering a continuance in this case outweigh the best interests of the public and Defendant's right to a speedy\ntrial, pursuant to 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 3161(h)(7)(A), (B)(i), and (B)(iv). Accordingly, the period of the exclusion shall be from March 16, 2020,\nthrough September 4, 2020. cc: USM, USPO. (LLR, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 07/09/2020)\n07/16/2020 104 MOTION for Hearing Letter by Tristan Grant. (PXS, COURT STAFF) Modified on 7/28/2020 to terminate motion. Hearing held 7/24/20.\n(BJK, COURT STAFF). (Entered: 07/17/2020)\n07/17/2020 103 MMS TEXT ORDER with SEALED VIRTUAL COURTROOM GUIDE as to Tristan Grant: Motion Hearing on MOTION for\nRelease from Custody re 101 -Bail Review Hearing set for 7/24/2020 at 01:00 PM in Virtual Courtroom 3 before Matthew McCrary\nScoble. A Status of Counsel Hearing will directly follow the Motion Hearing. (Attachments: # 1 Testing Connectivity) (JBO,\nCHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 07/17/2020)\n07/20/2020 105 Third Party Custodian Report (Sealed) as to Tristan Grant. (Johnson-Stewart, Alexandria) (Entered: 07/20/2020)\n07/24/2020 106 MINUTE ENTRY for proceedings held before Judge Matthew McCrary Scoble: Hearing on Motion for Release from Custody (DKT\n101)/Status of Counsel as to Tristan Grant held 1:01 p.m. to 1:04 p.m. and 1:23 p.m. to 1:24 p.m. on 7/24/2020. Court and counsel heard\nre video conferencing at this time; Defendant waived physical appearance and consented to telephonic appearance to protect human health\nand safety during the COVID-19 pandemic. Court and counsel heard re defendant's motion at Docket 101 release to third party custodian.\nCourt and counsel heard re motion to be withdraw without prejudice. Court and counsel heard re status of counsel. Court and counsel\nheard re there is no breakdown of relationship. Court and counsel heard re defendant's motion at Docket 101 ; DENIED without prejudice.\nTELEPHONIC APPEARANCES: Defendant present, in-custody (VTC); Kyle Frederick Reardon, AUSA; Steven M. Wells, CJA, Kyle\nMansfield, USPO; Sonja L. Reeves, Official Court Reporter (VTC). (IAH, COURT STAFF) Modified on 7/28/2020 to correct counsel for\ndefendant and regenerate nef.(BJK, COURT STAFF). (Entered: 07/24/2020)\n09/24/2020 109 MMS TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: A Status of Counsel Hearing is set for 10/9/2020 at 12:00 PM in Virtual Courtroom 2 before\nMatthew McCrary Scoble. Participating parties should refer to the attached sealed Courtroom Quick Guide for instructions. The court\nexpects all parties to appear via video conference unless they do not have video capabilities. To avoid delays, the court encourages counsel\nto assist and advise potential witnesses before the hearing about how to access the virtual courtroom by video. Only participating parties\nshould access the virtual courtroom. (JBO, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 09/24/2020)\n10/05/2020 110 RRB TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: A Telephonic Scheduling Conference is set for 10/23/2020 at 10:00 a.m. The parties shall\nattend by calling (866) 434-5269, Access Code 4591062, from a landline telephone five minutes prior to the start of the hearing. cc: USM,\nUSPO. (LLR, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 10/05/2020)\n10/09/2020 111 MINUTE ENTRY for proceedings held before Judge Matthew M. Scoble: Status of Counsel Hearing as to Tristan Grant held 12:02 p.m.\nto 12:05 p.m. and 12:21 p.m. to 12:23 p.m. on 10/9/2020. Defendant waived physical appearance and consented to appearance by video\nconference to protect human health and safety during the COVID-19 pandemic. Court and counsel heard re representation. Court relieved\ncounsel; CJA panel to appoint new counsel. VIRTUAL APPEARANCES: Defendant present, in-custody; Kyle Frederick Reardon, AUSA;\nSteven M. Wells, CJA. (HJR, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 10/09/2020)\n10/21/2020 114 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE: Brian D. Heady appearing for Tristan Grant (Heady, Brian) (Entered: 10/21/2020)\n10/23/2020 115 RRB TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: The telephonic scheduling conference set for October 23, 2020 at 10:00 a.m. is HEREBY\nVACATED. (RMC, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 10/23/2020)\n10/24/2020 116 MOTION to Withdraw as Attorney by Brian Heady. by Tristan Grant. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Heady, Brian) (Entered:\n10/24/2020)\n10/24/2020 117 AFFIDAVIT of Attorney by Tristan Grant 116 MOTION to Withdraw as Attorney by Brian Heady. filed by Tristan Grant (Heady, Brian)\n(Entered: 10/24/2020)\n10/26/2020 118 ORDER granting 116 Motion to Withdraw as Attorney. Brian D. Heady withdrawn from case. as to Tristan Grant (1). Signed by Judge\nRalph R. Beistline on 10/26/2020. (SDW, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 10/26/2020)\n10/26/2020 119 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE: James A. Wendt appearing for Tristan Grant (Wendt, James) (Entered: 10/26/2020)\n11/16/2020 120 RRB TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: A Telephonic Scheduling Conference is set for 11/19/2020 at 1:00 p.m. before Judge Ralph R.\nBeistline. The parties shall attend by calling (866) 434-5269, Access Code 4591062, from a landline telephone five minutes prior to the\nstart of the hearing. cc: USM, USPO. (LLR, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 11/16/2020)\n11/19/2020 121 MINUTE ENTRY for proceedings held before Judge Ralph R. Beistline: Scheduling Conference as to Tristan Grant held at 1:03 PM to\n1:22 PM on 11/19/2020. Defendant waived physical appearance and consented to appearance by telephone conference to protect human\nhealth and safety during the COVID-19 pandemic. Court and counsel heard re discovery and working on negotiations. Court found\nexcludable delay under 18 U.S.C. Section 3161(h)(7)(A) Continuance granted per (h)(7)(B)(iv) in order to give reasonable time to\nprepare. Court and counsel heard re defendant requesting a bench trial and request for status conference. Telephonic Status Conference set\nfor 12/23/2020 at 11:00 AM. Participating parties should call 866-434-5269, access code 4591062 five minutes prior to the start of the\nhearing. Court and counsel heard re setting TBC date, but TBC could change to a jury trial depending on upcoming MGOs. Trial by Court\nset for 1/25/2021 at 8:30 AM before Ralph R. Beistline in Anchorage with courtroom to be determined. Mr. Wendt to file Motion for\nBench Trial. TELEPHONIC APPEARANCES: Defendant present, in custody; Kyle Frederick Reardon, AUSA; James A. Wendt, CJA.\nOFF RECORD NOTE: Trial by Court set for 1/25/2021 at 8:30 AM is VACATED and RESET for 2/22/2021 at 8:30 AM before Ralph\nR. Beistline in Anchorage with courtroom to be determined. (LMH, COURT STAFF) Modified on 11/23/2020 to clarify text re TBC\nvacated on 1/25/2021 and regenerate NEF. (SDW, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 11/20/2020)\n12/02/2020 124 TRANSCRIPT of Proceedings as to Tristan Grant; Partial Transcript of Remote Proceedings Via Videoconference, Status of Counsel\nHearing (Public Proceedings) held on July 24, 2020 before Judge Matthew M. Scoble. Realtime Court Reporter: Sonja L. Reeves, RMR-\nCRR.\n\nAny party needing a copy of the transcript to review for redaction purposes may purchase a copy by calling Realtime Court Reporter,\nSonja L. Reeves, RMR-CRR (907) 677-6136. Transcript may be viewed at the court public terminal or purchased through the Transcriber\nbefore the deadline for Release of Transcript Restriction. After that date it may be obtained through PACER.\n\nThe parties have seven (7) calendar days to file with the court a Notice of Intent to Request Redaction of this transcript. If no such Notice\nis filed, the transcript may be made remotely electronically available to the public without redaction after Release of Transcript Restriction\ndeadline of 3/2/2021. Ordered by: James Wendt (SLR) (Entered: 12/02/2020)\n12/23/2020 127 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Ralph R. Beistline: Scheduling Conference as to Tristan Grant held at 11:13 a.m. to 11:45\na.m. on 12/23/2020. Defendant waived physical appearance and consented to appearance by telephone conference to protect human health\nand safety during the COVID-19 pandemic. The Court directed entry of the following Order: Pursuant to the Due Process Protections Act,\nthe Court confirms the United States obligation to produce all exculpatory evidence to the defendant pursuant to Brady v. Maryland, 373\nU.S. 83 (1963) and its progeny, and orders it to do so. Failing to do so in a timely manner may result in consequences, including, but not\nlimited to, exclusion of evidence, adverse jury instructions, dismissal of charges, contempt proceedings, or sanctions by the Court. Court\nand counsel heard re discovery, defendants intent to file Motion for TBC, and governments intent to file a response not opposing the\nmotion. Court and counsel heard re scheduling, TBC date, and pretrial memorandums. Pretrial memorandums due by 2/15/2021. In-person\nFPTC set for 2/18/2021 at 11:00 a.m. in Anchorage. Courtroom to be determined. Court and counsel heard re estimated trial length of 1\nweek, minors testifying at trial, and defendants intent to file a motion for a bail review hearing. Court found excludable delay under 18\nU.S.C. Section 3161(h)(7)(A) Continuance granted per (h)(7)(B)(iv) in order to give reasonable time to prepare. TELEPHONIC\nAPPEARANCES: Defendant present, in custody; Kyle Frederick Reardon, AUSA; James A. Wendt, CJA. (LMH, COURT STAFF) (SDW,\nCOURT STAFF). Modified on 2/20/2021 to attach MGO 21-03 as Main Document and regenerate NEF. (SDW, COURT STAFF)\n(Entered: 12/23/2020)\n12/23/2020 128 MOTION For Court Trial ON EXPEDITED CONSIDERATION by Tristan Grant. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Wendt, James)\n(Entered: 12/23/2020)\n12/28/2020 129 RRB TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: Plaintiff shall have until 12/31/2020 within which to respond to Defendant's Motion for Court\nTrial, filed at Docket 128 . It is so Ordered. (LLR, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 12/28/2020)\n12/31/2020 130 RESPONSE to Motion (Non-Opposition) by USA as to Tristan Grant 128 MOTION For Court Trial ON EXPEDITED CONSIDERATION\nfiled by Tristan Grant (Reardon, Kyle) Modified on 1/4/2021 to correct dkt text. (RMC, COURT STAFF). (Entered: 12/31/2020)\n01/04/2021 131 ORDER Regarding Court Trial as to Tristan Grant (1). Signed by Judge Ralph R. Beistline on 1/4/21. (LLR, CHAMBERS STAFF)\n(Entered: 01/04/2021)\n01/15/2021 132 NOTICE of 404(b) Evidence by USA as to Tristan Grant (Reardon, Kyle) (Entered: 01/15/2021)\n01/15/2021 133 NOTICE of Experts and Summary of Testimony by USA as to Tristan Grant (Reardon, Kyle) (Entered: 01/15/2021)\n01/20/2021 134 RRB TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: At docket 131, the Court granted Defendants request for a court trial to take place the week of\nFebruary 22, 2021, conditioned upon Defendants written waiver of his right to jury trial pursuant to Fed. R. Crim. P. 23(a)(1). To date, no\nsuch written waiver has been filed with the Court. A Telephonic Status Conference, therefore, is set for 1/21/2021 at 9:30 a.m. to address\nDefendant's intention in this regard. The parties shall attend by calling (866) 434-5269, Access Code 4591062, from a landline telephone\nfive minutes prior to the start of the hearing. It is so Ordered. (LLR, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 01/20/2021)\n01/21/2021 136 MINUTE ENTRY for proceedings held before Judge Ralph R. Beistline: Status Conference (Scheduling Conference) as to Tristan Grant\nheld 9:33 AM to 9:40 AM on 1/21/2021. Defendant waived physical appearance and consented to telephonic appearance to protect human\nhealth and safety during the COVID-19 pandemic. Court and counsel heard re defendant's outstanding TBJ waiver, defendant's intent to\nfile waiver by next week and parties intent to proceed with TBC in February. Court reminded parties that trial memos are due 2/15/21.\nTELEPHONIC APPEARANCES: Defendant present, in-custody; Kyle Frederick Reardon, AUSA; James A. Wendt, CJA; R. Joy Stancel,\nOfficial Court Reporter. (HJR, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 01/21/2021)\n01/25/2021 137 MOTION for Release from Custody ON SHORTENED TIME by Tristan Grant. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Wendt, James)\n(Entered: 01/25/2021)\n01/27/2021 138 MMS TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: MOTION for Release from Custody ON SHORTENED TIME re 137 is set as a Motion/Bail\nReview Hearing for 1/29/2021 at 03:30 PM in Anchorage Courtroom 2 before Matthew McCrary Scoble. Counsel should refer to the\nCourt's COVID-19 Court Operations Plan for details on in-person appearances and other important requirements at\nwww.akd.uscourts.gov/news/covid-19-coronavirus-and-court-operations. A public listening line is available via Virtual Courtroom 2 on\nthe Court website at https://www.akd.uscourts.gov/virtual-courtrooms. Participants are instructed to check virtual courtroom information\non the Court website for any updated connection information prior to the hearing date. (JBO, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 01/27/2021)\n01/28/2021 139 WAIVER of Right to Trial by Jury by Tristan Grant (Wendt, James) (Entered: 01/28/2021)\n01/28/2021 140 RESPONSE in Opposition by USA as to Tristan Grant re 137 MOTION for Release from Custody ON SHORTENED TIME (Reardon,\nKyle) (Entered: 01/28/2021)\n01/29/2021 141 NOTICE of Filing CD Conventionally by USA as to Tristan Grant re 140 Response in Opposition (Reardon, Kyle) (Entered: 01/29/2021)\n01/29/2021 142 Third Party Custodian Report (Sealed) as to Tristan Grant. (Johnson-Stewart, Alexandria) (Entered: 01/29/2021)\n01/29/2021 144 MMS ORDER as to Tristan Grant: The hearing scheduled for today at 3:30 PM has been CHANGED to VIRTUAL COURTROOM 1.\nAll other information remains the same (BJK, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 01/29/2021)\n01/29/2021 145 NOTICE of Supplemental Exhibit in Support of Government Opposition by USA as to Tristan Grant re 140 Response in Opposition\n(Reardon, Kyle) (Entered: 01/29/2021)\n01/29/2021 146 NOTICE of Filing CD Conventionally by USA as to Tristan Grant re 145 Notice (Other), 140 Response in Opposition (Reardon, Kyle)\n(Entered: 01/29/2021)\n01/29/2021 147 MINUTE ENTRY for proceedings held before Judge Matthew M. Scoble: Bail Review Hearing as to Tristan Grant held 3:39 PM to 4:13\nPM on 1/29/2021. Defendant waived physical appearance and consented to appearance by video conference to protect human health and\nsafety during the COVID-19 pandemic. Court and counsel heard re defendant's Motion for Release from Custody 137 . Arguments heard.\nDefendant's Motion for Release from Custody 137 ; DENIED. Court and counsel heard re defendant's difficulties reviewing discovery.\nCourt to follow-up with Marshals re computer time for discovery review. VIRTUAL APPEARANCES: Defendant present, in-custody;\nKyle Frederick Reardon, AUSA; James A. Wendt, CJA; Alexandria Johnson-Stewart, USPO (telephonic). (HJR, COURT STAFF)\n(Entered: 01/29/2021)\n02/01/2021 148 RRB TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: A Telephonic Status Conference is set for 2/5/2021 at 12:00 p.m. before Ralph R. Beistline.\nThe parties shall attend by calling (866) 434-5269, Access Code 4591062, from a landline telephone five minutes prior to the start of the\nhearing. cc: USM, USPO. (LLR, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 02/01/2021)\n02/02/2021 149 MMS ORDER as to Tristan Grant: Mr. Grant shall be given four (4) hours a day with an Alaska Dept. of Corrections laptop to review\ndiscovery. USMS shall inform D.O.C. of this Order. Joint Status Report due 2/5/2021. See Order for further details. Follows oral order of\n1/29/2021. Signed by Judge Matthew McCrary Scoble on 2/2/2021. (JBO, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 02/02/2021)\n02/03/2021 One CD and a chambers copy received and forwarded to Judge Scoble as to Tristan Grant 146 . (PXS, COURT STAFF) (Entered:\n02/03/2021)\n02/05/2021 151 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Ralph R. Beistline:Status Conference as to Tristan Grant held at 12:02 PM to 12:27 PM\non 2/5/2021. Defendant waived physical appearance and consented to appearance by video conference to protect human health and safety\n