 STAFF) (Entered: 02/11/2021)\n02/12/2021 166 MINUTE ENTRY for proceedings held before Judge Matthew M. Scoble: Hearing on Motion for Release from Custody as to Tristan\nGrant held 2:06 PM to 2:26 PM on 2/12/2021. Defendant waived physical appearance and consented to appearance by video conference to\nprotect human health and safety during the COVID-19 pandemic. Court and counsel heard re defendant's unopposed motion for release\n159 . Arguments heard. Defendant's unopposed motion for release 159 ; GRANTED. Defendant is to be released by 10:00 AM on 2/16/21,\n2/18/21 and 2/19/21 and self-remand no later than 5:00 PM each day. Mr. Wendt to contact the U.S. Marshals re remand. DQA to issue\nrelease order for each day. VIRTUAL APPEARANCES: Defendant present, in-custody; Kyle Frederick Reardon, AUSA (telephonic);\nJames A. Wendt, CJA (telephonic); Monte Hernandez, third-party custodian. (HJR, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 02/16/2021)\n02/12/2021 167 ORDER Setting Conditions of Release as to Tristan Grant signed by Judge Matthew McCrary Scoble on 2/12/2021. (HJR, COURT\nSTAFF) (Entered: 02/16/2021)\n02/12/2021 168 ORDER of Release as to Tristan Grant signed by Judge Matthew McCrary Scoble on 2/12/2021. (HJR, COURT STAFF) (Entered:\n02/16/2021)\n02/15/2021 161 TRIAL BRIEF by USA as to Tristan Grant (Reardon, Kyle) (Entered: 02/15/2021)\n02/15/2021 162 Proposed Jury Instructions by USA as to Tristan Grant (Reardon, Kyle) (Entered: 02/15/2021)\n02/16/2021 163 APPLICATION for Writ by USA as to Tristan Grant by USA (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Writ, # 2 Proposed Order)(Reardon, Kyle)\n(Entered: 02/16/2021)\n02/16/2021 164 APPLICATION for Writ by USA as to Tristan Grant by USA (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Writ, # 2 Proposed Order)(Reardon, Kyle)\n(Entered: 02/16/2021)\n02/16/2021 165 Notice of Intent to use the Court's Digital Evidence Presentation System (DEPS) for hearing/trial scheduled to begin 2/22/2021 by USA as\nto Tristan Grant (Reardon, Kyle) (Entered: 02/16/2021)\n02/17/2021 171 USPO Petition for Action on Conditions of Pretrial Release as to Tristan Grant. (CME, COURT STAFF) Modified on 2/18/2021 to remove\nsecurity and regenerate.(BJK, COURT STAFF). (Entered: 02/17/2021)\n02/17/2021 172 ORDER granting 171 USPO Petition for Action on Conditions of Pretrial Release. The petition, this order, and a copy of the warrant to be\ndisclosed only to the U.S. Attorney for their official use, until the arrest of the defendant. Clerk to issue Warrant of Arrest as to Tristan\nGrant (1). The petition for action is referred to the U.S. Magistrate Judge for pretrial release matters. Signed by Judge Matthew McCrary\nScoble on 02/16/2021. (CME, COURT STAFF) Modified on 2/18/2021 to remove security and regenerate nef. (BJK, COURT STAFF).\n(Entered: 02/17/2021)\n02/17/2021 173 ORDER granting Motions in Limine at 152 , 155 . Signed by Judge Ralph R. Beistline on 2/17/21. (LLR, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered:\n02/17/2021)\n02/17/2021 174 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE Jennifer Lowe Ivers appearing for USA. (Ivers, Jennifer) (Entered: 02/17/2021)\n02/17/2021 175 NOTICE OF DEFENDANT'S STATUS by USA as to Tristan Grant (Reardon, Kyle) (Entered: 02/17/2021)\n02/18/2021 Notice of Arrest of Tristan Grant defendant arrested 2/17/21. (BJK, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 02/18/2021)\n02/18/2021 176 MMS TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: Bail Review Hearing re 171 Petition for Action on Pretrial Release set for 2/19/2021 at 02:30\nPM in Virtual Courtroom 1 before Matthew McCrary Scoble. Participating parties should refer to the attached sealed Courtroom Quick\nGuide for instructions. The court expects all parties to appear via video conference unless they do not have video capabilities. To avoid\ndelays, the court encourages counsel to assist and advise potential witnesses before the hearing about how to access the virtual courtroom\nby video. Only participating parties should access the virtual courtroom. A public listening line for Virtual Courtroom 1 is available on the\nCourt website at https://www.akd.uscourts.gov/virtual-courtrooms. Counsel are instructed to check virtual courtroom information on the\nCourt website for any updated connection information prior to the hearing date. (BJK, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 02/18/2021)\n02/18/2021 177 MINUTE ENTRY for proceedings held before Judge Ralph R. Beistline: Status Conference (Final Pretrial Conference) as to Tristan Grant\nheld 11:01 AM to 11:32 AM on 2/18/2021. Court and counsel heard re possible conflict with Mr. Wendt and his investigator and speedy\ntrial issues. Court and counsel heard re Mr. Wendt's intent to file a Motion to Dismiss. Court and counsel heard re government's Oral\nMotion to continue trial; GRANTED. Trial scheduled for 2/22/21 is VACATED. Status Conference set 2/25/21 at 11:15 AM in virtual\ncourtroom 3 before Ralph R. Beistline. Court and counsel heard re trial scheduling and logistics, exhibits and witnesses and time for\ndefendant and attorney to confer. APPEARANCES: Defendant present; in-custody (VTC); Kyle Frederick Reardon, AUSA; Jennifer\nLowe Ivers, AUSA; James A. Wendt, CJA.\n\nOFF RECORD NOTE: Status Conference set 2/25/21 at 11:00 AM in virtual courtroom 3 before Ralph R. Beistline. (HJR, COURT\nSTAFF) (Entered: 02/19/2021)\n02/19/2021 178 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Matthew McCrary Scoble:Bail Review Hearing as to Tristan Grant held at 3:00 PM to\n3:08 PM on 2/19/2021. Defendant waived physical appearance and consented to appearance by video conference to protect human health\nand safety during the COVID-19 pandemic. Court and counsel heard re Petition for Action on Pretrial Release, TBC previously vacated,\nnew indictment, new counsel, and Status Conference set before Ralph R. Beistline next week. Court and counsel heard re no release plan\nat this time. Defendants detention continued. VIRTUAL APPEARANCES: Defendant present, in custody; Jennifer Ivers, AUSA; James A.\nWendt, DAT; Alexandria Johnson-Stewart, USPO. (LMH, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 02/22/2021)\n02/19/2021 179 ORDER OF DETENTION as to Tristan Grant Signed by Judge Matthew McCrary Scoble on 2/19/21. (LMH, COURT STAFF). Modified\non 2/22/2021 to attach order and regenerate (LMH, COURT STAFF). (Entered: 02/22/2021)\n02/25/2021 180 *AMENDED AT DKT 181* MINUTE ENTRY for proceedings held before Judge Ralph R. Beistline:Status Conference as to Tristan\nGrant held 11:02 a.m. to 11:24 a.m. on 2/25/2021. Defendant waived physical appearance and consented to telephonic appearance to\nprotect human health and safety during the COVID-19 pandemic. Court and counsel heard re defendant waive attorney conflict request,\nwitnesses and trial in April. Court ordered the Public Defender's Office to appoint counsel to confer with defendant. Court and counsel\nheard re setting a Status Conference 3/5/2021 at 9:00 a.m. Clerk's Office to check for availability. Parties will be notified of hearing date\nand time by separate order. VIRTUAL APPEARANCES: Defendant present, in-custody; Kyle Frederick Reardon, AUSA; Jennifer Lowe\nIvers, AUSA (telephonic); James A. Wendt, CJA. (IAH, COURT STAFF) Modified on 3/2/2021 to clarify text. (SDW, COURT STAFF)\n(Entered: 03/01/2021)\n03/02/2021 181 AMENDED MINUTE ENTRY: The parties are advised that the minute entry as to Tristan Grant: 180 Status Conference is amended as\nfollows: MINUTE ENTRY for proceedings held before Judge Ralph R. Beistline: Status Conference as to Tristan Grant held 11:02 a.m. to\n11:24 a.m. on 2/25/2021. Defendant waived physical appearance and consented to telephonic appearance to protect human health and\nsafety during the COVID-19 pandemic. Court and counsel heard re status of case and Mr. Wendt's oral motion to appoint conflict counsel;\nGRANTED; CJA Clerk notified. Court and counsel heard re defendant's intent to waive any conflict with counsel and waiver to be filed.\nTelephonic Status Conference to be set next week; Clerk's Office to check for availability; separate scheduling order to issue. VIRTUAL\nAPPEARANCES: Defendant present, in-custody; Kyle Frederick Reardon, AUSA; Jennifer Lowe Ivers, AUSA (telephonic); James A.\nWendt, CJA.\n\nOFF RECORD NOTE: Telephonic Status Conference set for 3/4/2021 at 12:00 PM in Remote Proceeding before Ralph R. Beistline. The\nparties shall attend by calling (866) 434-5269, Access Code 4591062, from a landline telephone five minutes prior to the start of the\nhearing. (SDW, COURT STAFF) Modified on 3/2/2021 to correct hearing date and regenerate NEF. (SDW, COURT STAFF) (Entered:\n03/02/2021)\n03/02/2021 182 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE: Samuel J. Fortier appearing for Tristan Grant Entry of Limited Appearance (Fortier, Samuel)\n(Entered: 03/02/2021)\n03/03/2021 183 NOTICE Notice to Court by Tristan Grant (Attachments: # 1 Declaration)(Fortier, Samuel) (Entered: 03/03/2021)\n03/04/2021 184 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Ralph R. Beistline:Scheduling Conference as to Tristan Grant held AT 12:10 PM to 12:30\nPM on 3/4/2021. Defendant waived physical appearance and consented to telephonic appearance to protect human health and safety\nduring the COVID-19 pandemic. Court and counsel heard re Mr. Fortier not present, conflict waiver and jury trial waiver, and trial by\ncourt. Court and counsel heard re civilian clothes not needed since there is no jury, defendants right to testify, courtroom to be open to the\npublic, and schedule for the TBC. Telephonic FPTC set for 4/6/21 at 10:00 AM before Ralph R. Beistline. The parties shall attend by\ncalling (866) 434-5269, Access Code 4591062, from a landline telephone five minutes prior to the start of the hearing. In-person TBC set\nfor 4/12/21 at 8:30 AM in Anchorage Courtroom 3 before Ralph R. Beistline. Motions in Limine to be filed by 3/29/21. Court and counsel\nheard re speedy trial. For the reasons stated in Miscellaneous General Order 21-05, the Court finds that the ends of justice served by\nordering a continuance in this case outweigh the best interests of the public and the defendant's right to a speedy trial, pursuant to 18\nU.S.C. \u00a7 3161(h)(7)(A), (B)(i), and (B)(iv). Absent further order of the Court, the period of exclusion shall be from 4/6/2021 through\n4/12/21. TELEPHONIC APPEARANCES: Defendant present, in-custody; Kyle Frederick Reardon, AUSA; Jennifer Lowe Ivers, AUSA\n(telephonic); James A. Wendt, CJA. (LMH, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 03/05/2021)\n03/09/2021 185 TRANSCRIPT REQUEST by Tristan Grant (Attachments: # 1 Exhibit, # 2 Exhibit, # 3 Exhibit, # 4 Exhibit, # 5 Exhibit, # 6 Exhibit, # 7\nExhibit)(Wendt, James) (Entered: 03/09/2021)\n03/09/2021 186 MOTION to Withdraw as Attorney by Samuel J. Fortier. by Tristan Grant. (Attachments: # 1 Supplement Declaration of Counsel, # 2\nProposed Order Order Authorizing Withdraw)(Fortier, Samuel) (Entered: 03/09/2021)\n03/09/2021 187 ORDER granting 186 Motion to Withdraw as Attorney. Samuel J. Fortier withdrawn from case as to Tristan Grant (1). Signed by Judge\nRalph R. Beistline on 3/9/21. cc: FPD (CJA clerk). (LLR, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 03/09/2021)\n03/31/2021 188 TRANSCRIPT of Proceedings as to Tristan Grant; Arraignment on Third Superseding Indictment held on October 23, 2019, before Judge\nMatthew M. Scoble.\nAny party needing a copy of the transcript to review for redaction purposes may purchase a copy from Realtime Court Reporter R. Joy\nStancel, by calling 907-677-6104. Transcript may be viewed at the court public terminal or purchased through the Transcriber before the\ndeadline for Release of Transcript Restriction. After that date it may be obtained through PACER.\n\nThe parties have seven (7) calendar days to file with the court a Notice of Intent to Request Redaction of this transcript. If no such Notice\nis filed, the transcript may be made remotely electronically available to the public without redaction after Release of Transcript Restriction\ndeadline of 6/29/2021. (RJS, ) (Entered: 03/31/2021)\n03/31/2021 189 TRANSCRIPT of Proceedings as to Tristan Gran