minal or purchased through the Transcriber before the\ndeadline for Release of Transcript Restriction. After that date it may be obtained through PACER.\n\nThe parties have seven (7) calendar days to file with the court a Notice of Intent to Request Redaction of this transcript. If no such Notice\nis filed, the transcript may be made remotely electronically available to the public without redaction after Release of Transcript Restriction\ndeadline of 7/19/2021. (RJS, ) (Main Document 232 replaced on 4/19/2021) (SDW, COURT STAFF). (Entered: 04/19/2021)\n04/19/2021 233 TRANSCRIPT of Proceedings as to Tristan Grant; Status Conference held on February 25, 2021, before Judge Ralph R. Beistline, District\nJudge.\nAny party needing a copy of the transcript to review for redaction purposes may purchase a copy by calling Realtime Court Reporter, R.\nJoy Stancel, 907-677-6104. Transcript may be viewed at the court public terminal or purchased through the Transcriber before the\ndeadline for Release of Transcript Restriction. After that date it may be obtained through PACER.\n\nThe parties have seven (7) calendar days to file with the court a Notice of Intent to Request Redaction of this transcript. If no such Notice\nis filed, the transcript may be made remotely electronically available to the public without redaction after Release of Transcript Restriction\ndeadline of 7/19/2021. (RJS, ) (Entered: 04/19/2021)\n04/19/2021 234 RRB TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: Having duly considered the United States' Motion for Extension of Time to File Response 224 ,\nthe motion is hereby GRANTED. The deadline to file is extended from the current due date of April 19, 2021, to April 23, 2021. (SDW,\nCOURT STAFF) Modified on 4/19/2021 to correct motion dkt number and regenerate NEF. (SDW, COURT STAFF) (Entered:\n04/19/2021)\n04/19/2021 235 RRB TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: Having duly considered the United States' Motion for Expedited Consideration 225 , the motion\nis hereby GRANTED. (SDW, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 04/19/2021)\n04/19/2021 236 TRANSCRIPT of Proceedings as to Tristan Grant; Trial by Court, Trial Day 1 held on April 12, 2021 before Judge Ralph R. Beistline.\nRealtime Court Reporter: Sonja L. Reeves, RMR-CRR.\n\nAny party needing a copy of the transcript to review for redaction purposes may purchase a copy by calling Realtime Court Reporter,\nSonja L. Reeves, RMR-CRR (907) 677-6136. Transcript may be viewed at the court public terminal or purchased through the Transcriber\nbefore the deadline for Release of Transcript Restriction. After that date it may be obtained through PACER.\n\nThe parties have seven (7) calendar days to file with the court a Notice of Intent to Request Redaction of this transcript. If no such Notice\nis filed, the transcript may be made remotely electronically available to the public without redaction after Release of Transcript Restriction\ndeadline of 7/19/2021. Ordered by: Kyle Reardon (SLR) (Entered: 04/19/2021)\n04/19/2021 237 TRANSCRIPT of Proceedings as to Tristan Grant; Partial Transcript of Trial by Court, Trial Day 2, Testimony of Ajela Banks held on\nApril 13, 2021 before Judge Ralph R. Beistline. Realtime Court Reporter: Sonja L. Reeves, RMR-CRR.\n\nAny party needing a copy of the transcript to review for redaction purposes may purchase a copy by calling Realtime Court Reporter,\nSonja L. Reeves, RMR-CRR (907) 677-6136. Transcript may be viewed at the court public terminal or purchased through the Transcriber\nbefore the deadline for Release of Transcript Restriction. After that date it may be obtained through PACER.\n\nThe parties have seven (7) calendar days to file with the court a Notice of Intent to Request Redaction of this transcript. If no such Notice\nis filed, the transcript may be made remotely electronically available to the public without redaction after Release of Transcript Restriction\ndeadline of 7/19/2021. Ordered by: Kyle Reardon (SLR) (Entered: 04/19/2021)\n04/20/2021 238 TRANSCRIPT REQUEST by USA as to Tristan Grant (Reardon, Kyle) (Entered: 04/20/2021)\n04/28/2021 239 TRANSCRIPT of Proceedings as to Tristan Grant; Partial Transcript of Trial by Court, Trial Day 2, Testimony of KC and JS held on April\n13, 2021 before Judge Ralph R. Beistline. Realtime Court Reporter: Sonja L. Reeves, RMR-CRR.\n\nAny party needing a copy of the transcript to review for redaction purposes may purchase a copy by calling Realtime Court Reporter,\nSonja L. Reeves, RMR-CRR (907) 677-6136. Transcript may be viewed at the court public terminal or purchased through the Transcriber\nbefore the deadline for Release of Transcript Restriction. After that date it may be obtained through PACER.\nThe parties have seven (7) calendar days to file with the court a Notice of Intent to Request Redaction of this transcript. If no such Notice\nis filed, the transcript may be made remotely electronically available to the public without redaction after Release of Transcript Restriction\ndeadline of 7/27/2021. Ordered by: Kyle Reardon (SLR) (Entered: 04/28/2021)\n04/29/2021 240 RESPONSE in Opposition by USA as to Tristan Grant re 209 MOTION to Dismiss for Violations of Speedy Trial Act (Reardon, Kyle)\n(Entered: 04/29/2021)\n04/30/2021 241 ORDER denying 209 Motion to Dismiss as to Tristan Grant (1). Signed by Judge Ralph R. Beistline on 4/30/21. (LLR, CHAMBERS\nSTAFF) (Entered: 04/30/2021)\n06/02/2021 242 DRAFT PRESENTENCE INVESTIGATION REPORT (Sealed) as to Tristan Grant. Objections to the Draft Presentence Report are due to\nthe Probation Officer and opposing counsel by June 16, 2021. Counsel should not rely on this draft for sentencing purposes. (Jedrosko,\nMatt) (Entered: 06/02/2021)\n06/15/2021 243 First MOTION to Continue Sentencing UNOPPOSED and ON SHORTENED TIME by Tristan Grant. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)\n(Wendt, James) (Entered: 06/15/2021)\n06/16/2021 244 RRB TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: Defendant's Unopposed First Motion to Continue Sentencing at Docket 243 is GRANTED. The\nImposition of Sentence Hearing set for 7/14/2021 is VACATED and RESET for 9/15/2021 at 9:00 a.m. in Anchorage Courtroom 4 before\nJudge Ralph R. Beistline. Sentencing memoranda are due seven days prior to the hearing. cc: USM, USPO. (LLR, CHAMBERS STAFF)\n(Entered: 06/16/2021)\n06/17/2021 245 MOTION FOR TEMPORARY RESTRAINING ORDER, LONG-TERM NO-CONTACT ORDER, AND TO RESTRICT\nCOMMUNICATIONS BY THE DEFENDANT by USA as to Tristan Grant. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order, # 2 Proposed Order, # 3\nProposed Order)(Ivers, Jennifer) (Entered: 06/17/2021)\n06/17/2021 246 AFFIDAVIT of APPLICATION FOR TEMPORARY RESTRAINING ORDER by USA as to Tristan Grant 245 MOTION FOR\nTEMPORARY RESTRAINING ORDER, LONG-TERM NO-CONTACT ORDER, AND TO RESTRICT COMMUNICATIONS BY\nTHE DEFENDANT filed by USA (Ivers, Jennifer) (Entered: 06/17/2021)\n06/23/2021 247 MMS TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: MOTION FOR TEMPORARY RESTRAINING ORDER, LONG-TERM NO-CONTACT\nORDER, AND TO RESTRICT COMMUNICATIONS BY THE DEFENDANT re 245 . The Court hereby GRANTS in part; and sets a 18\nU.S.C. \u00a7 1514(b)(1) evidentiary hearing for the long term no-contact order requested. Status of Counsel / Evidentiary / Motion Hearing set\nfor 6/24/2021 at 02:00 PM in Anchorage Courtroom 3 before Matthew McCrary Scoble. A written order for the temporary restraining\norder shall follow this Order. The temporary restraining order establishes the restrictions on Mr. Grant and Ms. Carter's contact with J.S.\nand family for 14 days from today. CJA to contact counsel for Ms. Carter in preparation of the hearing.(JBO, CHAMBERS STAFF)\n(Entered: 06/23/2021)\n06/23/2021 248 AMENDED ORDER as to Tristan Grant: This Order shall supersede the Order - Written Order Following Oral Order re 149 .\nDefendant's additional time to review discovery is hereby REVOKED. Additionally, access to telephone, mail, and Internet are\nRESTRICTED until further order of the court. USMS shall serve this Order on Mr. Grant and Alaska D.O.C. Signed by Judge Matthew\nMcCrary Scoble on 6/23/2021. (JBO, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 06/23/2021)\n06/23/2021 249 ORDER GRANTING TEMPORARY RESTRAINING ORDER as to Tristan Grant: Defendant shall not contact minor victim or her\nimmediate family members. See attached Order. USMS shall promptly file certification this Order was served on the Defendant\npersonally. Signed by Judge Matthew McCrary Scoble on 6/23/2021. (JBO, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 06/23/2021)\n06/23/2021 250 MOTION to Continue by USA as to Tristan Grant. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Ivers, Jennifer) (Entered: 06/23/2021)\n06/23/2021 251 MMS TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: Motion to Continue re 250 is GRANTED in part and DENIED in part. The hearing set for\n6/24/2021 at 2:00 PM will address the no-communication requested in the Motion; the long term no-contact request will be re-scheduled\nin due course. (JBO, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 06/23/2021)\n06/24/2021 252 MINUTE ENTRY for proceedings held before Judge Matthew M. Scoble: Hearing on Motion for Restraining Order/Status of Counsel\nHearing as to Tristan Grant held 2:04 PM to 2:07 PM and 2:25 PM to 2:41 PM on 6/24/2021. Court and counsel heard re Government's\nMotion for Temporary Restraining Order GRANTED at docket 249; hearing on Motion for Long-Term Restraining Order to be scheduled\nafter parties confer with witnesses. Court and counsel heard re parties to meet and confer re discovery and protected discovery. Court and\ncounsel heard re U.S. Marshals to follow-up with DOC re defendants lockdown status. APPEARANCES: Defendant present, in-custody;\nKayla Hayes Doyle, AUSA; James A. Wendt, CJA. (HJR, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 06/25/2021)\n07/07/2021 254 MMS TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: Parties are advised that the Temporary Restraining Order re 249 expires tomorrow, July 8,\n2021. Parties shall file a status report regarding the requests for the Longer Term No-Contact Order and Restriction on Communications\nby the Defendant re 245 . Status Report due by NOON on 7/8/2021. (JBO, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 07/07/2021)\n07/08/2021 255 STATUS REPORT by USA as to Tristan Grant (Ivers, Jennifer) (Entered: 07/08/2021)\n07/08/2021 256 STATUS REPORT Defendant's Supplemental Status Report by Tristan Grant (Wendt, James) (Entered: 07/08/2021)\n07/09/2021 257 MMS TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: The Court has reviewed both Status Reports re 255 & 256 . A Motion Hearing on MOTION re\n245 is set for 7/13/2021 at 12:00 PM to 1:00 PM in Anchorage Courtroom 4 before Matthew McCrary Scoble; and [if necessary] for\n7/16/2021 at 10:00 AM to 1:00 PM in Anchorage Courtroom 1 before Matthew McCrary Scoble. The court finds good cause to extend\nthe Temporary Restraining Order and No Contact Order until the Court has the opportunity to hear evidence and make a determination\nregarding the Long-Term Restraining order. USMS shall notify AK DOC of the extension of the No Contact Order and Temporary\nRestraining Order until the next hearing on 7/13/2021. cc: USMS, Clerks/DQA (JBO, CHAMBERS STAFF) (Entered: 07/09/2021)\n07/12/2021 258 MMS TEXT ORDER as to Tristan Grant: Due to courtroom availability, for the [if necessary] continued "
